160 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(Alibaba's latest AI release, Qwen 2.5-max, comes at a crucial time when DeepSeek has put intense pressure on major players. Alibaba's response, dropping a new model on the first day of the lunar new year, makes it clear that they're feeling the heat.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[0]/P 97 0 R>>
endobj

161 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(WHAT'S THE BIG DEAL?)/E(WHAT'S THE BIG DEAL?)/Pg 10 0 R/K[5]/P 97 0 R>>
endobj

162 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(Alibaba claims Qwen 2.5-Max surpasses DeepSeek's latest model, Chat GPT's GPT-4o, and Meta's newest Llama-3.1-405B model. Alibaba clearly needs a win after DeepSeek's low-cost AI disrupted the market, and Qwen 2.5-Max remains their solution. )/Pg 10 0 R/K[6]/P 97 0 R>>
endobj

163 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(Their Mixture-of-Experts \(MoE\) model allows for a more efficient approach than standard LLMS, allowing faster inference speeds and lower computational costs. Although MoEs aren't new \(with most models using them\), some use MoEs sparingly while using traditional LLMs. In contrast, Alibaba's new Qwen model is fully built around MoE technology, lowering the cost of Alibaba's Qwen for optimisation. )/Pg 10 0 R/K[7]/P 97 0 R>>
endobj

