341 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(HOW MUCH ENERGY DOES CHAT GPT ACTUALLY USE?)/E(HOW MUCH ENERGY DOES CHAT GPT ACTUALLY USE?)/Pg 20 0 R/K[8]/P 107 0 R>>
endobj

342 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(A common belief is that a single ChatGPT query consumes ten times more power than a single google search, how true is the general belief that AI consumes a lot of energy?)/Pg 20 0 R/K[2]/P 107 0 R>>
endobj

343 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(Recent analysis suggests it may be lower than what we initially believed. Older estimates used outdated hardware GPUs to make predictions and as we\220ve gradually continue predictions, many researchers have failed to account for improvements and implemented optimisation techniques. )/Pg 20 0 R/K[3]/P 107 0 R>>
endobj

344 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(Optimisation techniques that exist because the company wants to save money; companies like OpenAI, Google or Meta actively invest it techniques not just for user improvement to be reduce costs through energy consumption. Optimisations from batch processing \(grouping queries together to utilise GPU efficiency\), hardware improvements and using MoE models can drastically cut costs on a larger scale. )/Pg 20 0 R/K[4]/P 107 0 R>>
endobj

345 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(Current estimates calculate energy usage through tokens \(see page x for more\), short standard text based queries average around 0.3 watt-hours or. )/Pg 20 0 R/K[9]/P 107 0 R>>
endobj

346 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(However, with longer input queries \(related to books or articles\), this can skyrocket; )/Pg 20 0 R/K[10]/P 107 0 R>>
endobj

347 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(a 10,000 token input \(short paper or article\) can be around 2.5 watt-hours)/Pg 20 0 R/K[11]/P 107 0 R>>
endobj

348 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(A 100,000 token input \(around 200 pages\) can be around 40 watt hours )/Pg 20 0 R/K[12]/P 107 0 R>>
endobj

349 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(For reference, 0.3 Watt-hours equates to using a single LED build for roughly a minute while 40 watt hour is similar to fully charging a smartphone about 2.5 times. While individual ChatGPT queries are relatively low in energy consumption, the real drain comes from the initial training phase of large AI models.)/Pg 20 0 R/K[13]/P 107 0 R>>
endobj

