448 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(Although continuously improved, no matter how advanced, LLM models will be shrouded with the same issues due to the fundamental pattern recognition they\220re built on rather than true understand. Pattern recognition essentially means matching and predicting based on huge dataset, identifying correlations and forming patterns while not understanding the meaning behind them. For example, LLMs can generate human-like text due to their training but they cannot fully \217understand\220 the concepts they\220re discussing. )/Pg 25 0 R/K[11]/P 112 0 R>>
endobj

449 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(World models can adapt through their own learning and interaction with the real world, for example reacting instantly to new situations, for example, a self-driving care can\220t just rely on pattern recognition of traffic signs but would need to understand the context, for example predicting a future movements or adjusting to weather changes, none of which can be achieved through pattern recognition alone. )/Pg 25 0 R/K[12]/P 112 0 R>>
endobj

450 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 112 0 R/Pg 25 0 R/K[18]>>
endobj

451 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 112 0 R/Pg 25 0 R/K[19]>>
endobj

452 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(HOW ARE WORLD MODELS CONNECTED TO AGI?)/E(HOW ARE WORLD MODELS CONNECTED TO AGI?)/Pg 25 0 R/K[13]/P 112 0 R>>
endobj

453 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(World models are considered a major stepping stone towards AGI due to the prioritisation of attempting to mimic how humans perceive and understand the world, in order to be classified as AGI, world models need a combination of advanced memory systems, real world interaction and the ability to self-improve. AGI as we understand it would require self-awareness, a model that functions entirely on some level of prediction wouldn\220t fit this definition.  )/Pg 25 0 R/K[14]/P 112 0 R>>
endobj

454 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(Self-awareness in AGI refers to the capacity of the machine to recognise itself in its environment, its goals and internals state. This expands to meta-cognition in humans which refers to reflection on thoughts, biases recognition and a deeper understanding of motivation. World models may not fit the definition of AGI in its early stages due to its primary focus being on understanding and predicting the environment rather than its own goals and internal state. Would models may be able to simulate cause-and-effect relationships in the world, but may not necessarily have a way of understanding themselves or reflecting on their own actions.)/Pg 25 0 R/K[15]/P 112 0 R>>
endobj

