617 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(AI CAN IDENTIFY GENDER THROUGH EYE SCANS, BUT NO-ONE KNOWS HOW. )/E(AI CAN IDENTIFY GENDER THROUGH EYE SCANS, BUT NO-ONE KNOWS HOW. )/Pg 33 0 R/K[7]/P 120 0 R>>
endobj

618 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 120 0 R/Pg 33 0 R/K[17]>>
endobj

619 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(A recent study by the university of Malaysia found that AI can a accurately determine gender from retinal images with a 96% accuracy rate. Human experts cannot currently reliably identify gender from eyeballs alone; unlike facial structure, bone density or proportions, eyeballs themselves have no sexual difference with male and female eyes being nearly the same in shape and size. It begs the question, what can AI see that humans can\220t?)/Alt()/Pg 33 0 R/K[6]/P 120 0 R>>
endobj

620 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(AI\220S ABILITY TO SEE THE INVISIBLE )/E(AI\220S ABILITY TO SEE THE INVISIBLE )/Pg 33 0 R/K[11]/P 120 0 R>>
endobj

621 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(Retinas appear structurally identical between male and females with no clear difference in blood vessels or macula, yet AI detects these hidden patterns suggesting deep learning can sometimes extract subtle data that traditional analysis methods overlook. )/Alt()/Pg 33 0 R/K[12]/P 120 0 R>>
endobj

622 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(WHY THIS MATTERS FOR MEDICINE)/E(WHY THIS MATTERS FOR MEDICINE)/Pg 33 0 R/K[13]/P 120 0 R>>
endobj

623 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(If AI can detect gender-specific retinal features, it could help detect other things we can\220t see at a much earlier stage; subtle biological differences or diagnosis of conditions such as Alzheimers and diabetes. Alzheimer\220s identification would be useful as of right now, we\220re unable to efficiently identify Alzheimer\220s disease at its early stage as it lacks clear biomarkers, AI detecting these changes could signal its development before traditional methods can.  )/Alt()/Pg 33 0 R/K[14]/P 120 0 R>>
endobj

